    "body": "When you preview a post from the Reader using the 🌏 icon, you get a preview of the site itself. However, some elements (especially fixed ones like cookie-related banners) are hidden behind the bottom bar and cannot be used.\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\nTo be able to access all the elements from the in-app preview.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nThe bottom overlay bar gets on top of important elements like the button to accept/deny cookies:\r\n\r\nhttps://zerowastechef.com/ | https://rafaelfunchal.com.br/ | https://toddhensonphotography.com/\r\n------------ | ------------- | -------------\r\n<img src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1136160/111379368-d0633d80-8681-11eb-9963-996c04058633.png\"/> | <img src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1136160/111379384-d48f5b00-8681-11eb-9f47-83141636b596.png\"/> | <img src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1136160/111379389-d5c08800-8681-11eb-91b8-9d6c6d5fa41b.png\"/>\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce the behavior\r\n\r\n1. Open the Reader\r\n2. Open a post from a site with one of these bottom banners. Examples: https://toddhensonphotography.com/blog, https://zerowastechef.com/, or https://rafaelfunchal.com.br/\r\n3. Tap the globe icon to preview the site\r\n4. Check the bottom\r\n\r\n##### Tested on iPhone 7, iOS 14.4, WPiOS 16.8.0.4\r\n\r\nReported also in 3826878-zen\r\n",
